1
00:44:26,693 --> 00:44:30,477
- Oh, may we take it into another room?
- Yes, to the sun room in the back.

2
00:44:30,507 --> 00:44:32,754
- Thank you, give me a hand.
- Excuse me.

3
00:44:42,689 --> 00:44:44,709
Oh, Warner, where have you been?

4
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:48,478
Well madame, it would
have been an accident?

5
00:44:48,674 --> 00:44:50,649
There's been a murder.

6
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:56,060
Mark Fleming, the young man from whom I
leased this place is killed here tonight.,

7
00:44:56,973 --> 00:45:00,342
- They know who did it?
- Well they, they believe it was the Bat.

8
00:45:00,372 --> 00:45:03,229
I'm sorry I had to use the
front door Miss Van Gorder.

9
00:45:03,259 --> 00:45:05,233
Bu I forgot my keys
and when I rang the bell

10
00:45:05,257 --> 00:45:07,231
at the kitchen door,
there was no response.

11
00:45:07,488 --> 00:45:11,664
Oh, this is Warner Lieutenant.
He's my butler, he was my chauffeur.

12
00:45:12,599 --> 00:45:13,624
Why did you promote him?

13
00:45:13,654 --> 00:45:17,348
Well, it's very difficult to find a butler
they don't like service in the country.

14
00:45:18,388 --> 00:45:19,940
Have you been a butler before?

15
00:45:20,317 --> 00:45:24,490
I've served in many capacities sir, but
this was my night off and I forgot my keys.

16
00:45:24,491 --> 00:45:25,384
I heard that part.

17
00:45:26,379 --> 00:45:27,711
What time you leave the house tonight?

18
00:45:27,989 --> 00:45:30,912
Oh, about 6:30, I had
dinner at Wiley's roadhouse.

19
00:45:31,716 --> 00:45:33,701
Can you prove where you
spent the rest of the evening?

20
00:45:34,451 --> 00:45:36,544
- I can try.
- Try hard.

21
00:45:37,517 --> 00:45:39,409
And don't leave the
house, I'll get to you later.

22
00:45:39,711 --> 00:45:40,854
Very good sir.

23
00:45:41,195 --> 00:45:43,945
I shall be in my room Miss
Van Gorder, if you need me.

24
00:45:44,849 --> 00:45:45,729
Yes Warner.

25
00:45:48,418 --> 00:45:50,164
Surely, you don't think he's...

26
00:45:51,261 --> 00:45:52,883
Warner and I met before.

27
00:45:54,020 --> 00:45:56,515
I can't recall where or when.

28
00:45:57,889 --> 00:45:58,824
But I will.

29
00:46:04,416 --> 00:46:06,255
There'll be a crew
here shortly from headquarters...

30
00:46:06,285 --> 00:46:08,155
dusting for fingerprints,
taking photographs.

31
00:46:08,958 --> 00:46:10,210
But in the meantime...

32
00:46:11,082 --> 00:46:13,577
Miss Patterson, you aren't
leaving the house tonight are you?

33
00:46:13,941 --> 00:46:14,968
No Lieutenant.

34
00:46:15,477 --> 00:46:16,852
Don't, I'll talk to you in the morning.

35
00:46:17,193 --> 00:46:17,633
Good night.

36
00:46:18,073 --> 00:46:20,375
- Good night sir.
- Good night Miss Patterson.

37
00:46:21,418 --> 00:46:22,384
Dale...

38
00:46:23,180 --> 00:46:25,051
I was with Mark Fleming
this afternoon when you...

39
00:46:25,081 --> 00:46:26,874
talked to him about
the floor plans of this house.

40
00:46:27,394 --> 00:46:29,132
I heard him tell you he
was coming here tonight.

41
00:46:29,422 --> 00:46:31,776
Dale called him at my request.

42
00:46:32,548 --> 00:46:34,262
She told me he was coming.

43
00:46:35,095 --> 00:46:36,351
Who else heard her tell you that?

44
00:46:37,220 --> 00:46:41,855
- Judie, Lizzie...
- And that nice Dr. Wells..

45
00:46:42,072 --> 00:46:43,231
Dr. Wells?

46
00:46:46,961 --> 00:46:49,061
There are few killers
who kill for the fun of it.

47
00:46:49,942 --> 00:46:53,372
The Bat very likely is a mental case and I'm
convinced that his crimes are motivated...

48
00:46:53,402 --> 00:46:55,778
by his, mainly personal gain.

49
00:46:56,293 --> 00:46:57,922
There's a million dollars at large.

50
00:46:58,187 --> 00:47:01,217
And he's going to keep on hunting
for it until he lays his hands on it.

51
00:47:02,002 --> 00:47:03,921
Now, these young ladies
are staying here tonight?
